### The key idea

I would organize the entire dashboard around **four questions**:

| Question                           | Dashboard capability                   |
| ---------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| **Is the platform healthy?**       | DC/dependency health                   |
| **Is business processing moving?** | volume, throughput, backlog            |
| **What is wrong?**                 | error trends + attention queue         |
| **What do I do?**                  | root cause + impact + remediation hint |

And for your platform specifically, make **Pending Amount, Settlement Reconciliation, Error Code + Root Cause, Processing Backlog, and Multi-DC Ownership/Recovery** first-class metrics. Those will provide considerably more value to Ops/support than a dashboard dominated by generic infrastructure graphs.


